    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` to the v2 export API.\n\n**Changes**\n- Switched from `GET /v1/payouts` to `GET /v2/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` across overlapping windows until `drained: true`.\n- Deduplicates payouts by `id`, since adjacent windows repeat the boundary payout.\n- Retries `429` responses with the identical request after honoring `Retry-After`.\n- Handles `400 invalid_cursor` by restarting the export once from the beginning.\n- Added optional `--limit`; existing `--base-url` and `--out` behavior is unchanged.\n\n**Verification against `http://the VM's public address:18080`**\n- Ran the updated script with both `--limit 100` and the default window size.\n- Result: `synced 2431 payouts`\n- Validation:\n  - `2431` rows, `2431` unique ids\n  - Required payout fields present\n  - Creation order preserved\n  - Exact id match with the live v1 endpoint: no missing or extra payouts\n- The server did emit `429 Too Many Requests` during paging; the retry logic handled them and the export completed.",
